  "cli_result_text": "Submitted 25 files spanning the three repos, ordered by relevance to the listener-container threading refactor:\n\n**spring-kafka** (primary implementation surface):\n- `ConcurrentMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the target concurrency model (wraps N `KafkaMessageListenerContainer`s)\n- `KafkaMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 the single-threaded container being delegated to\n- `AbstractMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 shared base class (lifecycle, error handlers, executor wiring)\n- `MessageListenerContainer.java` / `GenericMessageListenerContainer.java` \u2014 core container contract (bridges to spring-framework's `SmartLifecycle`)\n- `ContainerProperties.java` \u2014 carries `listenerTaskExecutor`, ack-mode, and other concurrency-relevant settings\n- `config/ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `AbstractKafkaListenerContainerFactory.java`, `KafkaListenerContainerFactory.java` \u2014 factory chain that builds containers for `@KafkaListener` endpoints\n- `annotation/EnableKafka.java`, `KafkaListenerAnnotationBeanPostProcessor.java`, `KafkaBootstrapConfiguration.java`, `config/KafkaListenerEndpointRegistry.java` \u2014 annotation-driven registration path\n- Existing concurrency test suites (`ConcurrentMessageListenerContainerTests.java`, `...MockTests.java`) for the risk/breaking-change assessment\n\n**spring-boot** (autoconfiguration/properties consumer):\n- `KafkaAutoConfiguration.java`, `KafkaAnnotationDrivenConfiguration.java` \u2014 autoconfigures the listener container factory\n- `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer.java` \u2014 maps `spring.kafka.listener.*` properties onto the factory/container\n- `KafkaProperties.java` \u2014 owns the `concurrency` property exposed to users\n\n**spring-framework** (core abstractions spring-kafka builds on):\n- `SmartLifecycle.java`, `Lifecycle.java`, `DisposableBean.java` \u2014 container lifecycle contract\n- `AsyncTaskExecutor.java`, `TaskExecutor.java`, `SimpleAsyncTaskExecutor.java` \u2014 the threading executor abstraction each child container uses to run its poll loop\n\nThis confirms the dependency chain the task describes: spring-framework's `TaskExecutor`/`SmartLifecycle` abstractions underpin spring-kafka's container hierarchy, and spring-boot's autoconfiguration/properties layer sits strictly on top of spring-kafka's factory API \u2014 so the refactor ordering (framework \u2192 kafka \u2192 boot) is structurally forced, with the concurrency-related config surface (`KafkaProperties.Listener.concurrency` \u2192 `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactoryConfigurer` \u2192 `ConcurrentKafkaListenerContainerFactory`) being the main coupling point to preserve compatibility across.",
